## Description
As an Alkemio user I want to be able to have huge whiteboards without any problems

## Context
Current whiteboard preview generation relays on two browser functions: `Canvas.toBlob` and `URL.createObjectURL`
There's a limitation on browsers, some are failing when running `toBlob` on very big canvases.

Excalidraw also has a `scale` parameter to export whiteboards resized. At the moment this parameter is used to increase the scale of the whiteboard if it's too small. We could use this or maybe resize the canvas once exported.

I haven't been able to find a table with the limits per browser, but I have run a test script (attached at the bottom):
Firefox - Linux - i7 32GB RAM : Max 24000x24000pixels
Chromium - Linux - i7 32GB RAM : Max 17000x17000pixels

This is more of a Spike to see if we can use a different function or to scale the canvas when it's too big, or use Excalidraw's scale.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Whiteboard preview doesn't fail - not even with huge whiteboards

## Additional Context
Screen shots / UX designs / data that are relevant.

```
(function () {
  let size = 1000;

  const step = () => {
    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = size;
    canvas.height = size;

    try {
      canvas.toBlob(
        blob => {
          if (blob) {
            size += 1000;
            step();
          } else {
            console.log('toBlob returned null at size:', size);
          }
        },
        'image/png'
      );
    } catch (err) {
      console.log('toBlob threw at size:', size, err);
    }
  };

  step();
})();
```

