The problem lays on a member user (space member, not admin of anything), not able to upload files on certain storageBuckets.

Spaces have a StorageAggregator with a few storageBuckets:
```graphql
{
  lookupByName{
    space(NAMEID:"testspacea"){
      id
      storageAggregator{
        directStorageBucket{
          ...sb
        }
        storageBuckets{
          ...sb
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fragment sb on StorageBucket {
    id
    parentEntity {
      id
      type
      displayName
    }
    documents {
      id
      displayName
    }
    authorization{
       myPrivileges
    }
}
```

- **directStorageBucket**: not used at all. and that's good, only used in administration and accounts for very specific things
- space > **profile** > storageBucket - **was not used at all**. It is going to be where we store temporary Callout files while creating a Callout
- space > **about** > profile > storageBucket - **Everything** is going into this storageBucket. Both MUI and CRD
- space > about > **guidelines** > profile > storageBucket - **Not used at all**
- space > collaboration > **innovationFlow** > profile > storageBucket - **Not used at all**


So, before the bugfix, everything temporary in a space was going to the space's about StorageBucket, which I think it's wrong, and with "everything" I mean:
- Temporary images in the markdown of a callout description when creating a callout (callout edit works well)
- Temporary references when creating a callout
- Images in the markdown of the community guidelines
- Images in the markdown when editing an Innovation flow state
- ... maybe/probably more


There's also a setting in the space: `allowMembersToCreateCallouts`. 
The problem is that members (not-admins of the space), don't have `FILE_UPLOAD` permission on the SpaceAbout storage bucket. so when they are creating a callout, any temporary file upload (attach image to the description or add a reference) fails with an error. In MUI we solved this just hiding image attachment on markdown editor.

What the fix does:
- Instead of uploading images to the SpaceAbout's StorageBucket, now CreateCallout dialog uploads images to the Space's StorageBucket (it was not used at all in the past, it first came to exist when the actors migration).
- Added a permission to the Space's StorageBucket so members can UPLOAD_FILE when the setting `allowMembersToCreateCallouts` is ON.

What to test:
- Check permissions of the Space's StorageBucket and the About's StorageBucket for admins and non admins when `allowMembersToCreateCallouts` is ON and off:
| Role | Space's StorageBucket | About's StorageBucket |
  |------|----------------------|----------------------|
  | Admin | READ, FILE_UPLOAD | READ, FILE_UPLOAD |
  | Member — allowMembersToCreateCallouts ON | READ, FILE_UPLOAD | READ |
  | Member — allowMembersToCreateCallouts OFF | READ | READ |

- Test that you can upload images to the callout descriptions, and add references. as admin and as a member, and that they go to the Space's storage bucket and not to the SpaceAbout's storageBucket.
- Test that we always have the ability to upload images/references, not like in MUI
-

What's missing/for the future:
- CommunityGuidelines form is uploading to About's SB, when it has its own SB. Easy to modify, but I'm worried that the anonymous users may not have access to read files from it, so not touching anything for now. Server is not moving files to the CG's SB either
- InnovationFlow form is uploading to About's SB, and it also has its own SB. Server is also not moving the files to the correct SB. Also left for untouched. For the future.
- Create templates form is using About's too - it works because to create template you need to be admin anyway. In this case server is correctly moving the files to the Template's SB when created, so I think it would be more correct to use Space's but it can stay as is.
- Calendar event's are also using About's - same as before, uploaded to About's but correctly moved after creation.
- Another unrelated issue I just detected: Members have file-upload permission to the InnovationFlow's SB no matter the space settings. As far as I've seen. This is probably a bug, would need to dig a bit more to be sure.

