**Describe the bug**
The pagination functionality yields wrong results when a cursor is used.

Timebox: half a day

### Example 1
```graphql
{
  activityFeed {
    total
    pageInfo {
      startCursor
      endCursor
      hasNextPage
      hasPreviousPage
    }
    activityFeed {
      id
    }
  }
}
```
This query returns (below), which has the correct `start` and `end` but wrong `hasPreviousPage` because this must be the first page of all pages and wrong `hasNextPage` because there are no more than 20 records in the database.
```json
{
  "data": {
    "activityFeed": {
      "total": 20, // correct
      "pageInfo": {
        "startCursor": "bbcff673-13fa-4e28-982c-ad1cfb8cfc95", // correct
        "endCursor": "eea2f313-3df7-4c01-9a5e-24a152f1748f", // correct
        "hasNextPage": true, // incorrect
        "hasPreviousPage": true // incorrect
      },
      "activityFeed": [
        {
          "id": "bbcff673-13fa-4e28-982c-ad1cfb8cfc95"
        },
        {
          "id": "b75789c0-6b95-4008-94a7-9721df0cec37"
        },
       // 17 more ...
        {
          "id": "eea2f313-3df7-4c01-9a5e-24a152f1748f"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
### Examples 2
```graphql
{
  activityFeed(first:1, after:"7c1ac17b-f19d-491a-b03b-4cf892e3e9ce") {
    total
    pageInfo {
      startCursor
      endCursor
      hasNextPage
      hasPreviousPage
    }
    activityFeed {
      id
    }
  }
}
```
This query returns (below), which all wrong. The correct record after `7c1ac17b-f19d-491a-b03b-4cf892e3e9ce` is `b75789c0-6b95-4008-94a7-9721df0cec37`(see data for example 1).
```json
{
  "data": {
    "activityFeed": {
      "total": 20, // correct
      "pageInfo": {
        "startCursor": null, //incorrect
        "endCursor": null, //incorrect
        "hasNextPage": false, //incorrect
        "hasPreviousPage": false //incorrect
      },
      "activityFeed": [] //incorrect
    }
  }
}
```

Having name property in @Field overrides the in code variable name. This is likely a nest bug.
See example below:
```
@ArgsType()
export class StorageBucketArgsDocuments {
  @Field(() => [UUID_NAMEID], {
    name: 'IDs',
    description: 'The IDs or NAMEIDS of the Documents to return',
    nullable: true,
  })
  IDs?: string[];

  @Field(() => Float, {
    name: 'limit',
    description:
      'The number of Documents to return; if omitted return all Documents.',
    nullable: true,
  })
  limit?: number;
}
```
If we were to refactor the IDs variable name without changing the name property and vice versa we would end up with a bug.

Suggested fix: search all usage of @ArgsType() and remove name property of `Field` decorator.

